            can be endowed with a (left-) Hopf module structure, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            a Hopf algebra, simply by tensoring with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is given as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi h
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi h
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi h
                  %mo ′
                  %mi h
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho: h'\otimes h\otimes v\mapsto h'h\otimes v
          %p and the coaction as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi h
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma: h\otimes v\mapsto \Delta(h)\otimes v
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo :
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta:H\to H\otimes H
            the comultiplication. This is known as a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong trivial Hopf module
          %p
            The fundamental theorem of Hopf modules states that
            %em any
            Hopf module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            arises precisely in this way, as one shows that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mtext co
                      %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M\cong H \otimes M^{\text{co} H}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mtext co
                      %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi H
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{\text{co} H}:= \{m\in M \vert \sigma(m)= 1_H \otimes m\}
            is the space of coinvariant of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            under the coaction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V \mapsto H\otimes V
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mtext co
                      %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M\mapsto M^{\text{co} H}
          %p
            come as functors realizing an equivalence of categories between vector spaces, and
            = succeed "-Hopf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a{:href => "#Vercruysse12"} Vercruysse 2012
            for more on this).
